---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="M.S. Thesis">
  <section class="frame" style="padding-top: 40px;">
    <div class="grid-margin">
      <div class="margin-col">M.S. THESIS<br/>IIT MADRAS<br/>2022&ndash;2025</div>
      <div>
        <h1 style="font-size: 2rem;">Establishing UAVs as a viable alternative to weather balloons</h1>

        <p style="margin-top: 20px; max-width: 560px;">
          Weather balloons are the standard tool for profiling the lower atmosphere, but
          they drift with the wind, can only be launched once, and give a single vertical
          slice of data. This thesis built a hexacopter-based system that flies a repeatable
          path and measures the same quantities &mdash; wind speed, temperature, pressure and
          humidity &mdash; directly, using a custom sensor hub.
        </p>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 32px;">What the system does</h3>
        <ul style="max-width: 560px; color: var(--ink);">
          <li>Converts body-frame wind measurements to inertial-frame wind profiles</li>
          <li>Predicts weather-balloon trajectories computationally, for comparison against UAV data</li>
          <li>Reaches up to 2 km altitude on the atmospheric-sampling variant</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 32px;">Hardware</h3>
        <p style="max-width: 560px;">
          Two airframes were built over the course of the project: an early quadcopter,
          then a hexacopter purpose-built for ship-based takeoff and landing (2 kg payload,
          45-minute endurance), and later an advanced hexacopter reaching 10 kg payload,
          60-minute endurance and 5 km altitude capability.
        </p>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 32px;">Field deployments</h3>
        <div style="display:flex; gap: 32px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 12px;">
          <div><div class="stat">INS Rajali</div><div class="stat-label">testing &amp; validation</div></div>
          <div><div class="stat">ORV Sagar Kanya</div><div class="stat-label">Arabian Sea</div></div>
          <div><div class="stat">ORV Sagar Nidhi</div><div class="stat-label">Bay of Bengal</div></div>
          <div><div class="stat">Rameshwaram</div><div class="stat-label">coastal missions</div></div>
        </div>
        <p style="margin-top: 16px; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--slate);">
          Photos and flight data from each site are going up on the
          <a href="/campaigns/">campaigns page</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
